title: 'pallet-revive: fix eth_getLogs with empty address/topic filter lists'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    An `eth_getLogs` filter with an empty address list (`"address": []`) or an empty topic
    list at a position (`"topics": [[]]`) built an invalid `IN ()` SQL clause, causing the
    query to fail. Such filters are valid Ethereum requests and, as in other Ethereum
    clients, an empty list now imposes no constraint (it matches any address/topic) instead
    of erroring.
crates:
- name: pallet-revive-eth-rpc
  bump: patch
